WEBVTT

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.070
Play!

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.540
H-Hey, Taiga's...

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.220
Isn't that lead a little too wide!?

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.000
Yeah.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.960
<i>"We don't have the option of taking such huge risks"?</i>

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.170
<i>I was waiting for them to miss!</i>

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:26.510
What!?

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.610
Out!

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.690
Hey, you,

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.550
your senses aren't bad,

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.440
but you should be a little more humble against us.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.130
<i>Now I get it.</i>

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:50.400
<i>It's still far away from home plate.</i>

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:32.080
Strike!

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.140
Batter out!

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:35.410
All right! One down! One down!

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:38.070
All right! Keep it up!

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:42.560
Although we're leading, we haven't had an inning without a leadoff hit yet.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.920
Be more reliable, come on!

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:50.210
Batting first: center fielder, Kusano-kun.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.010
Play!

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:07.890
C-Crap! The no-run, no-hit inning is gone already!

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.220
<i>You were aiming for that?</i>

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.160
We finally got a hit in.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.120
Batting second: second baseman, Tokashiki-kun.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:24.310
He's running!

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:29.440
Safe!

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.990
<i>Damn it, they're completely hemming us in.</i>

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.950
<i>Even with Shigeno's speed and my arm,</i>

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.450
<i>they've all been able to get to second base with one hit.</i>

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.920
<i>He'll try to get third too, so you better be careful, Shigeno!</i>

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:46.840
<i>And he doesn't even use his pickoff move!</i>

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:49.300
Safe!

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.620
One out and a runner on third:

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:56.890
It's the same situation as the previous inning.

00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:01.770
They seem to be strictly aiming to score their runs this way.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.690
<i>These guys just don't learn.</i>

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:17.370
<i>Realize that you can't score runs with the squeeze anymore!</i>

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.110
Ball!

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:29.930
<i>Did you think that ridiculous method would work on us twice?</i>

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:34.390
<i>If we just leave it alone, it'll be four balls.</i>

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:40.590
<i>Well, that's only if the catcher can keep catching those pitches.</i>

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:46.640
Back! Back!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.780
That was close.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:55.610
As I thought, since we don't know where a ball in the dirt will bounce, it's not so useful.

00:04:56.990 --> 00:05:00.210
In the end, it's a shallow strategy.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:02.310
That's too dangerous, Shigeno.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.460
Don't throw balls in the dirt anymore.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:06.150
The opponent knows when we'll use it too.

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:09.170
At this rate, we'll just end up giving them four balls or have a passed ball!

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:13.340
Anyway, there's one out and you have three balls;
you should only throw to strike them out.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.090
Even if they try a squeeze,

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:18.050
it might not succeed with your pitches.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:20.920
Wait a second, Tashiro.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:23.720
I have an idea.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.370
Didn't I say it earlier?

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:29.160
I won't get caught up in their pace.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:35.920
I'll teach them that their baseball manual won't score runs against us anymore.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:42.450
Now that they're nervous about getting a passed ball,
they can't throw balls in the dirt anymore.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.680
We've got them now.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:49.070
They'll still use the squeeze after all, eh?

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:50.690
And it's one out with three balls...

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:53.380
Honda-kun doesn't have much of a choice but to pitch a strike.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:58.040
Kaido couldn't have found a better time to use the squeeze.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:01.680
Play!

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:04.600
<i>Let's do this, Tashiro!</i>

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:16.190
Idiot.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:17.610
<i>It's loose!</i>

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:20.070
No! Go back, Kusano!

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:23.330
What?

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:27.710
Here's the payback for tricking Taiga in the previous inning!

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:31.790
Out! Out!

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.550
T-They did it!

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:36.300
All right!

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:46.320
To make the ball bounce right in front of Shigeno-kun...

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:49.730
The runner can't get back with that.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:54.190
<i>Is it really okay that it went so well!?</i>

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:00.590
Sheesh! That guy's pretty lucky.

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:01.760
That's not it.

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:06.880
He was luring out Kusano in the first place.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:11.580
He made it look like they missed the ball when it hit the catcher's protective gear.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:15.420
Either way, it was Kusano's mistake.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:18.740
Now we can't tell who's the veteran team.

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:21.590
Egashira-san.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.050
We should change our attack pattern soon.

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:28.310
They're not opponents that common sense will work on.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.980
Batting third: third baseman, Yakushiji-kun.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.370
Do you have the confidence?

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:46.160
Are you saying you have the confidence to break past him?

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:49.370
Yes, of course.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:53.210
The only thing I'm worried about in this game...

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:57.630
is the possibility of the rain washing away a game we've already won.

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:02.030
Play!

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.640
Is it really okay to hold the bat so far down!?

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.310
Strike!

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:19.980
You're so carefree, even though you didn't even try to hit it.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:23.740
That's not cool at all!

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:32.960
Is it foul!?

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.120
Fair!

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:48.040
Two outs with a runner on first and third...

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.260
And next is...

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:55.440
Batting fourth: catcher, Sato-kun.

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:03.420
What was that? Did Yakushiji use some weird batting form?

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:05.320
D-Did he?

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:17.120
<i>It's just before the game, so what does Sato want with us?</i>

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:18.920
<i>Who knows?</i>

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:20.630
<i>But, he should be here soon.</i>

00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:24.620
<i>Sorry I'm late.</i>

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.970
<i>I had some trouble getting this recording.</i>

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:37.450
<i>What? Isn't this Shigeno's previous game?</i>

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:39.920
<i>We saw this at the meeting already.</i>

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:43.360
<i>I analyzed his pitches on my own.</i>

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:52.830
<i>In his best condition, we'd get a hit against him once every three innings, or at worst, once every four innings.</i>

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.670
<i>Hey, you make us sound pretty pathetic.</i>

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:58.430
<i>It's not like I'm underestimating 150km/h pitches, but...</i>

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.840
<i>it's not that hard to hit them, is it?</i>

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:02.800
<i>Did you forget?</i>

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:08.950
<i>None of us have been able to hit his pitches in the past.</i>

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:12.510
<i>Directly fighting him is too dangerous.</i>

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:17.770
<i>Therefore, I tried to find a weakness in his pitches,</i>

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:20.240
<i>although it was fruitless at first.</i>

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.340
<i>"At first"?</i>

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:22.480
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:24.420
<i>I found it.</i>

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:27.450
<i>A decisive way to bring him down.</i>

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.530
<i>Why are you telling just us?</i>

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:33.780
<i>Why?</i>

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:37.200
<i>I thought you'd be the only ones who could make use of this with your skills.</i>

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:45.880
This is a free fansub.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:45.880
Not for sale or rent.

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:53.930
Foul! Foul!

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:04.200
<i>What was that just now!?</i>

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:09.590
<i>He purposely hit that pitch outside...</i>

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:13.280
<i>That's not a pitch you want to swing at to start off.</i>

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:14.890
Play!

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:19.460
Even if you hit that pitch, it'll only be a foul!

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:21.670
Strike!

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:27.660
<i>What?</i>

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:30.370
<i>A blank pitch that loses spin?{nuketekuru shoot kaiten no boudama da to!?}{blank pitch = boudama. Not really sure if there's a certain word for it... it's basically a pitch with nothing special to it. An ordinary/regular pitch}</i>

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:31.350
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:33.100
<i>This pitch is just like that.</i>

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:37.130
<i>The one when Karasawa hit the homerun...</i>

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.310
<i>Normally, the ball would seem slower because of the gyro's spin, but...</i>

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:45.260
<i>once it goes inside and leaves the strike zone,
it becomes a blank pitch.</i>

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:46.190
<i>What!?</i>

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:51.150
<i>The gyroball's effectiveness depends on delicate balance and accuracy.</i>

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:57.120
<i>So if the pitcher gets fatigued, or the balance is broken slightly, it loses its spin and becomes a blank pitch.</i>

00:11:57.510 --> 00:12:00.430
<i>Are you saying Shigeno throws blank pitches?</i>

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:02.540
<i>Only once in five or six.</i>

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:06.960
<i>Furthermore, it's quite apparent that the amount of those pitches increase during the latter half of the game.</i>

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:11.590
<i>Wait, if he had pitches like that, wouldn't he get hit more often?</i>

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:15.050
<i>A no-hit shutout is just impossible.</i>

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:17.510
<i>He's just lucky.</i>

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:21.020
<i>The loose, blank pitches just end up as balls.</i>

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:25.730
<i>No player swings when they know it's a ball, right?</i>

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:29.310
<i>Then why aren't you telling the others about this?</i>

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:31.650
<i>Wouldn't it be best to let them know?</i>

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.450
<i>No, there's a risk to that.</i>

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.950
<i>Hitting a bad ball could ruin the batter's form.</i>

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:40.620
<i>Since the game will reach a stalemate at some point,{akumade tsuukaten ni suginai kono shiai dakedo}</i>

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:43.180
<i>it'd be pointless if everyone does that.</i>

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:43.910
<i>So...</i>

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:47.830
<i>Just the three of us, who are at the top of the order, will hit those loose pitches.</i>

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.300
<i>Sorry, Goro-kun.</i>

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:53.870
<i>Your wild idea that Seishuu Private had the possibility of winning with your pitching...</i>

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.840
<i>It's about time to put an end to it!</i>

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:00.270
Foul!

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:06.650
Foul!

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:15.540
As I thought, Honda's energetic pitches aren't easy, even for Toshiya-kun.

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:16.910
Actually,

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:19.870
Toshiya-kun seems to be cutting them on purpose.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:25.330
<i>This one!</i>

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.580
I-It's out!

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:48.520
Amazing...

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:55.660
That one was just like the first pitch, one that would've ended up as a ball.

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:59.940
It looks like they've found a way to break past Shigeno-kun.

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:06.630
<i>I see.</i>

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:12.080
Splendid work, Sato.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.050
Thank you.

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:19.000
Out!

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:21.390
Three outs! Change!

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:24.430
They're going for the loose pitches?

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:30.180
Yeah, looking at that fifth batter,
I don't think all of them are doing it.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:32.400
Yakushiji and Sato?

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:38.050
Now that I think about it, Kusano also hit one in the first inning.

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:42.900
They all ended up as balls, so I hadn't been worrying about them until now.

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:45.420
Well, that's how it is.

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:47.630
We've got a way to handle this too.

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:53.140
Besides that, we have to do something about those four runs.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:57.460
Top of the fourth inning: leading off for Seishuu High School...

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:00.130
Batting second: third baseman, Uchiyama-kun.

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:02.100
Play!

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:05.390
<i>The rain's gotten stronger.</i>

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:08.320
<i>Let's hurry up and end this.</i>

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:15.480
Out!

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.680
So they do make it easy to hit on purpose...

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:21.790
We're counting on you, Shigeno!

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:25.770
Batting third: pitcher, Shigeno-kun.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.240
Amazing as usual, Toshi.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:35.210
Since you can't hit my pitches head on, you purposely aim for my loose ones.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:39.580
I don't know where your pride or courage have gone, but...

00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:44.390
if that's the difference between us after a year,

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:49.020
then I really can't let you guys win this game.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:58.160
Strike!

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:02.120
With four runs,

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.660
did you think I'd cave in!?

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:20.260
Out!

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.580
He's not in control.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.420
He's overdoing it.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:37.360
Should we just pray for the rain to start pouring now?

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:42.250
Shigeno...

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:46.030
Batting fourth: catcher, Tashiro-kun.

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:54.560
Ball!

00:16:58.200 --> 00:16:59.140
Ball!

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:00.130
Four balls!

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:01.300
All right!

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:03.540
All right!

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:06.580
Kaido threw four balls...

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:08.600
Well, it's good for us, isn't it?

00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:12.500
What's wrong?

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:15.170
There's nothing to get nervous about here, is there?

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:18.520
No, the rain is just a little hard on my control.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:21.480
My legs aren't really handling it well either.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:26.230
Well, we can let them hit for now.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:29.870
If we stay laid back, a game cancelled due to rain would be troublesome.

00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:30.660
Yeah.

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:34.230
Batting fifth: second baseman, Fuji-kun.

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:35.620
Bring it!

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:42.200
Ball!

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:45.810
Excuse me, can you please change the ball?

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:47.590
But I just changed it earlier...{Lloyd: I'm not sure what we've done in the past when an umpire is just regulary talking and not giving calls}

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:49.050
Please, change it.

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:50.850
O-Okay.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:01.770
Ball!

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:08.280
Fuji! Don't worry about it!

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:09.490
Just be bold!

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:13.350
<i>I-Idiot! Don't say that so casually!</i>

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:16.080
<i>Do you think I can hit that slider so easily!?</i>

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:18.610
Look, the pitcher's weakening!

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:23.000
<i>You...</i>

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:24.510
<i>Crap!</i>

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:30.680
This is...

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:32.560
All right!

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:35.890
It's the rain.

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:37.800
Rain?

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:41.050
Ichihara is pretty sensitive.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.310
This rain is taking away his rhythm.

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:48.530
Looks like the heavens are starting to show up on our side.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:51.600
Ball!

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:52.950
Hattori!

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.260
<i>Calm down, Ichihara.</i>

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:05.750
Ouch!

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:07.820
Dead ball!

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:15.110
T-The bases are loaded!

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:16.890
Could this be...?

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:19.850
They're doing pretty well.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:24.310
<i>He becomes so disorderly when it rains like this?</i>

00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:27.280
All right! It's our chance, Miyazaki!

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:28.640
Stay calm!

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:31.310
Just whack it and run with all you've got!

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:32.990
O-Okay.

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:40.080
It's really started to pour!

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.040
T-Time out! Time out!

00:19:49.690 --> 00:19:51.930
The energy was nice and high...

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:54.830
Just when I finally contributed...

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:56.430
Huh? Where's Shigeno?

00:19:57.320 --> 00:20:00.340
For now, we'll watch the conditions for another 10 minutes,

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:04.450
and if the weather doesn't get better, we'll have to cancel the game.

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:08.230
Well, they're currently in the lead, so...

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:10.870
I don't have a problem with starting again on another day.

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:12.440
Don't be ridiculous.

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:18.410
The weather was clearly predicted to be bad today, wasn't it?

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:23.670
Restarting a game like this, all the way from the beginning again, is a waste of time.

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:29.690
As long as we can resume, Kaido can wait 30 minutes or even an hour.

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:34.680
If an unfavorable decision is made during that time,

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:39.830
we'll be forced to consider sending a protest to the committee.

00:20:44.490 --> 00:20:46.860
Good words there, daddy's boy!

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:49.070
N-Nogoro-kun!

00:20:49.070 --> 00:20:52.310
I agree with resuming! Completely agree!

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:59.590
Well, who knows if you'd have been better off stopping the game now, when we'll make you cry later.

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:02.750
The rain...

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:07.210
It's letting up!

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:11.170
They're resuming?

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:16.720
We'll see who'll get the better end of this.

00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:20.140
In a situation like this, their high energy has been disrupted.

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:24.100
Seishuu has lost the good luck it finally had.

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:28.560
Too bad the game didn't get cancelled for you.

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.980
What are you saying, Goro-kun?

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:34.200
You're losing 4-0, you know.

00:21:34.590 --> 00:21:38.160
You're the one hanging on by a thread now that the game isn't cancelled.

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:43.320
We're the ones who wouldn't be happy if we had to redo the game.

00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:46.080
Who's hanging on by a thread?

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:48.550
It's a good turn of events.

00:21:48.550 --> 00:21:52.430
If we were guys who'd give up after just four runs,

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:54.550
it'd just be the same if we redid it!

00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:58.390
Do you think I'd stand for stopping this midway?

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:04.430
Bottom of the fourth inning: Seishuu has two outs and the bases are loaded.

00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:05.480
Resume the game!

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:11.810
Strike!

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:14.330
He's back, that Ichihara.

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:18.280
Yeah, the rain let up, and they put more dirt on the mound.

00:22:18.750 --> 00:22:22.520
Besides that, he probably got a chance to cool down.

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:26.030
Strike!

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:27.920
Do something, Miyazaki!

00:22:27.920 --> 00:22:29.550
If you don't swing, you won't hit it!

00:22:32.250 --> 00:22:36.420
On top of having to resume, the pitcher's back on his feet...

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:39.130
When it rains, it pours.

00:22:51.500 --> 00:22:52.730
Safe! Safe!

00:22:53.310 --> 00:22:54.690
All right!

00:22:57.580 --> 00:22:58.650
All right!

00:22:58.650 --> 00:23:00.990
All right! We got a run back!

00:23:02.110 --> 00:23:03.440
<i>Look at that!</i>

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:08.930
<i>We still haven't lost sight of the goddess of victory!</i>

00:24:40.620 --> 00:24:43.590
It's Team Seishuu's counterattack!

00:24:43.590 --> 00:24:45.720
We'll get those three runs back!

00:24:45.720 --> 00:24:49.140
The rest will be up to me to hold them down.

00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:51.390
In order to win against Kaido, I'll...

00:24:52.350 --> 00:24:53.730
Next time, on Major:

00:24:53.730 --> 00:24:54.980
Direct Challenge.

00:24:55.440 --> 00:24:57.690
Run to the stage of your dreams!
